---
/**
 * Orders.
 *
 * Built around the question that actually gets asked: "somebody has emailed
 * saying they cannot find their tickets, can you look them up". So the search
 * box is the first thing on the page and it matches on anything the customer
 * might quote.
 *
 * The `event` and `q` query parameters are read here so the dashboard and
 * gig list can deep-link straight into a filtered view.
 */
import AdminLayout from '@/layouts/AdminLayout.astro';
import DataTable from '@/components/admin/DataTable.astro';
import StatusBadge from '@/components/admin/StatusBadge.astro';
import StatCard from '@/components/admin/StatCard.astro';
import AdminIcon from '@/components/admin/AdminIcon.astro';
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button.astro';
import EmptyState from '@/components/ui/EmptyState.astro';
import ScaffoldNote from '@/components/ui/ScaffoldNote.astro';
import { getPaymentDiscrepancies, getServices } from '@/services/index.ts';
import { formatPence } from '@/lib/money.ts';

const services = getServices();

const eventId = Astro.url.searchParams.get('event') ?? '';
const query = Astro.url.searchParams.get('q') ?? '';

const gigs = await services.admin.listAll();
const selected = eventId ? gigs.find((g) => g.id === eventId) : undefined;

const orders = query
  ? await services.orders.search(query, eventId || undefined)
  : eventId
    ? await services.orders.listForEvent(eventId)
    : await services.orders.listRecent(60);

// AMPED-07D2-3: money SumUp may be holding that is attached to no order.
// Surfaced here because this is the page an operator is already on when a
// customer says they have paid and have no ticket.
const openDiscrepancies = await getPaymentDiscrepancies().countOpen();

const paid = orders.filter((o) => o.order.status === 'paid');
const gross = paid.reduce((sum, o) => sum + o.order.totalInPence, 0);
const ticketCount = paid.reduce((sum, o) => sum + o.ticketCount, 0);
---

<AdminLayout
  title="Orders"
  subtitle={
    selected
      ? `Orders for ${selected.title}. Search by name, email, order number or ticket reference.`
      : 'Search by name, email, order number or ticket reference.'
  }
  wide
>
  <form class="order-filter" method="get" action="/admin/orders">
    <div class="order-search">
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="order-q">Search orders</label>
      <input
        id="order-q"
        name="q"
        type="search"
        value={query}
        inputmode="search"
        placeholder="Name, email, AMP-26-00814, or a ticket reference"
      />
      <AdminIcon name="search" size={20} class="order-search-icon" />
    </div>

    <label class="visually-hidden" for="order-event">Filter by gig</label>
    <select id="order-event" name="event">
      <option value="">All gigs</option>
      {
        gigs.map((gig) => (
          <option value={gig.id} selected={gig.id === eventId}>
            {gig.title} - {gig.shortDateLabel}
          </option>
        ))
      }
    </select>

    <Button type="submit" variant="solid" size="md">Search</Button>
    {(query || eventId) && <Button href="/admin/orders" variant="ghost" size="md">Clear</Button>}
  </form>

  <div class="order-stats">
    <StatCard label="Orders shown" value={orders.length} detail={query ? 'Matching your search' : 'Most recent first'} />
    <StatCard label="Paid" value={paid.length} tone="go" detail={`${ticketCount} tickets`} />
    <StatCard label="Value" value={formatPence(gross)} tone="volt" detail="Paid orders shown" />
    <StatCard
      label="Needs a look"
      value={orders.filter((o) => o.order.status === 'awaiting_payment' || o.order.status === 'refunded').length}
      detail="In checkout or refunded"
      tone="warn"
    />
    <StatCard
      label="Payment discrepancies"
      value={openDiscrepancies}
      detail={
        openDiscrepancies === 0
          ? 'All payments accounted for'
          : 'Require attention'
      }
      tone={openDiscrepancies > 0 ? 'stop' : 'go'}
      href="/admin/discrepancies"
    />
  </div>

  {
    orders.length > 0 ? (
      <DataTable caption="Ticket orders">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Reference</th>
            <th scope="col">Customer</th>
            <th scope="col">Gig</th>
            <th scope="col">What they bought</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">Total</th>
            <th scope="col">Status</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">In</th>
            <th scope="col">Placed</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {orders.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="mono">{row.order.reference}</td>
              <td>
                {row.order.customerName}
                <span class="dim block">{row.order.customerEmail}</span>
              </td>
              <td>
                <a href={`/admin/gigs?highlight=${row.order.eventId}`}>{row.eventTitle}</a>
              </td>
              <td>
                {row.order.items.map((item) => (
                  <span class="block">
                    {item.quantity} &times; {item.ticketTypeName}
                  </span>
                ))}
                {row.order.status === 'paid' && row.tickets.map((ticket) => (
                  <a class="block" href={`/admin/tickets/${ticket.id}`}>View {ticket.reference} QR</a>
                ))}
              </td>
              <td class="num">{row.totalLabel}</td>
              <td>
                <StatusBadge kind="order" status={row.order.status} />
              </td>
              <td class="num">
                {row.checkedInCount}/{row.ticketCount}
              </td>
              <td class="dim">{row.placedLabel}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </DataTable>
    ) : (
      <EmptyState
        title={query ? 'Nothing matches that' : 'No orders yet'}
        body={
          query
            ? 'Try just the surname, or the first part of the email address. Order references look like AMP-26-00814.'
            : 'Orders appear here as soon as somebody buys a ticket.'
        }
        actionHref="/admin/orders"
        actionLabel="Clear the search"
      />
    )
  }

  <ScaffoldNote slice="AMPED-08B">
    Partially refunded orders require manual review at the door. Automatic ticket-level admission
    remains disabled until a later refund slice records which purchased unit was refunded.
  </ScaffoldNote>
</AdminLayout>

<style>
  .order-filter {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
  }

  .order-search {
    position: relative;
  }

  .order-search input {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 3rem;
    padding: var(--s-2) var(--s-3) var(--s-2) 3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline-strong);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    background: var(--ink-inset);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .order-search input:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--volt);
  }

  .order-search-icon {
    position: absolute;
    left: var(--s-3);
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    color: var(--text-faint);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .order-filter select {
    min-height: 3rem;
    padding: var(--s-2) var(--s-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline-strong);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    background: var(--ink-inset);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .order-stats {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .block {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--step--2);
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .order-filter {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 16rem auto auto;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .order-stats {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
